WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.869
-You know our first guests
tonight from their work

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:07.106
as Olivia Benson and Elliot
Stabler on "Law &amp; Order: SVU"

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:10.710
as well as the latest spin-off,
"Law &amp; Order: Organized Crime."

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.878
You can see both shows
beginning Thursday nights

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:14.246
at 9:00 here on NBC.

00:00:14.246 --> 00:00:15.315
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:17.216
Mariska Hargitay
and Christopher Meloni.

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:19.452
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:26.592 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:33.699 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:40.840 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.709
Welcome back, both of you!

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.077
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:47.213
-Wow!

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.915
-You say our names backstage
to announce us,

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:51.551
the crowd's reaction.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.353
She turns to me, she goes,
"We've still got it."

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:55.287
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:58.057
-Well, and I should say.
I should say.

00:00:58.057 --> 00:00:59.925
-We still got it.
-I think you --

00:00:59.925 --> 00:01:01.994
I think you both
independently have it,

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:03.562
but I think
there's an extra excitement

00:01:03.562 --> 00:01:05.565
that you're here together, so
thank you so much for making --

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.069
And I should also note,
you were --

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.503
this was planned a while ago.

00:01:11.503 --> 00:01:12.738
There were some
scheduling issues

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:14.139
and you guys had to back out.

00:01:14.139 --> 00:01:16.008
And you have such intense fans,

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:17.976
a lot of them took it out on me
on social media.

00:01:17.976 --> 00:01:19.345
-No!
-They did.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.947
It was as if, last minute,
I decided I didn't want you.

00:01:21.947 --> 00:01:23.616
[ Laughter ]
-That's great, though.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.385
This is perfectly us.
You go, "No!"

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.753
And I was thinking,
"Better you than me."

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:28.121
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.756
Is this too casual, by the way?
-No, I think it's lovely.

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:33.592
-Not the dress but my posture.
-It's a little casual.

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:35.627
-Okay, great.
-What I wanted to say is

00:01:35.627 --> 00:01:41.167
our fans are crazy, crazy loyal
and they're so nuts.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.369
I don't think other people
have fans like we do.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:45.904
I'm not ribbing on your fans.
I'm sure they're great.

00:01:45.904 --> 00:01:50.175
I'm just saying the "SVU" fans
are -- They're hard-core.

00:01:50.175 --> 00:01:54.446
-And you know, there's a very --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:54.446 --> 00:01:57.383
There's the thinnest of veneer
between you and your fans

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.351
when you film a show
that is often outdoors

00:01:59.351 --> 00:02:00.620
in New York City, right?
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.088
-You see fans a lot.
They feel very close to you.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:03.856
They have made art
based on you guys.

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:06.225
-They have made art.
-A beautiful mug, Christopher.

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:07.694
You sent us a picture.
Can I show this?

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.562
And I mean,
just to get the likeness right

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:11.664
on a mug like this.
-It's not easy.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:12.765
-I mean, it is --

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.900
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.135
I mean, when you...

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.104
-Spit in it.
-Yeah.

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.007
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.675
-I've had that for 20 years.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:23.976
-Have you really?
-Yeah.

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:25.812
-'Cause it looks like it just
came out of the box.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:26.712
-I know.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:27.813
Right out of the kiln.

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:29.381
-Right out of the kiln.
And look at that.

00:02:29.381 --> 00:02:30.616
That's really nice, too,

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.651
'cause you do have such
a beautiful profile.

00:02:32.651 --> 00:02:35.421
-And a strong chin.
-Strong chin.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.156
-Big nose, strong chin.
-That's like a double shot

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:38.724
of espresso when you have that
in the morning.

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:40.593
-Every morning.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.328
Also, people have referenced,
when the two of you

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:45.831
are together, and again this
is just on my social media,

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:48.834
Chriska or Chrishka.

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:50.869
-It's Chrishka.
-Chrishka, thank you.

00:02:50.869 --> 00:02:52.071
[ Cheers and applause ]
-It's Chrishka.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.039
Oh, yeah, we're Chrishka.
-That's really nice.

00:02:54.039 --> 00:02:55.675
-Yeah, it's beautiful.
-Or Bensler.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.745
-Bensler. Is it Bensler?
-Yeah.

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.413
-Chrishka and Bensler.
-Oh, Bensler and Chrishka.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.547
Okay, great.

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:02.748
-There was a new one
that just happened.

00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:04.483
Oh, Marshmelon.

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:05.818
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.453
-Marshmallow?

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.955
-Chris calls me Marsha
sometimes.

00:03:09.955 --> 00:03:11.557
-Gotcha.
-One of the many names.

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:13.525
-Now, last time you were here,
you were here with Ice-T.

00:03:13.525 --> 00:03:14.660
Did you want to
come out to prove

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.163
that you guys have
better chemistry?

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.197
-No.
-Okay.

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:21.700
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.703
I want to --
Alright, so, the show, 23 years.

00:03:24.703 --> 00:03:26.572
-Wait, I want to show what
my fans did for me.

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:28.407
-What did they do?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:30.042
-Did you bring it?
-Yes, I did.

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:31.910
-"But what about me?"
-Oh, yeah, they did. I'm sorry.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.946
-Yeah, because look.
-Okay, I apologize.

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:35.515
-So, there's three.
-Okay.

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:37.550
-Guys?
[ Audience awws ]

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.951
Come on, all I ever wanted.

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:40.086
-They're voodoo dolls.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.787
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:43.956
-All I ever wanted was a doll
named after me.

00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:46.325
-I think we only have two.
-No, there's three.

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:48.628
Just saying, if you didn't --
-He wants to keep one.

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:51.697
-My fans are gonna be so mad
that you didn't have the third.

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:53.666
-This is all I have down there.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.801
-How about this?
And look at the hair. Whoo!

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.603
-If there's one backstage,
we'll have it

00:03:57.603 --> 00:03:58.871
'cause we'll do two acts
with you guys.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.439
So if we find the third one,
we'll bring it out.

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:02.441
But I will be honest. Can I just
say something, Mariska?

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:04.577
Don't take it the wrong way.
If it looks just like these two,

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:05.912
I don't know
if we needed to show it.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.313
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.248
-I hear you, but the other one
was the first one.

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:11.784
It's a frownie face doll.
-Okay, gotcha, alright.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:14.220
Alright. So I want to ask,
you had done --

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.421
I knew you first from "Oz."

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.022
You had done a couple episodes
of "E.R."

00:04:17.022 --> 00:04:19.092
When you read
the pilot for "SVU,"

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:21.126
what were your first reactions
to it?

00:04:21.126 --> 00:04:24.630
-It was called "Sex Crimes."
-Yeah, I remember.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:30.369
-I literally went, "Okay,"
as did my mother because once --

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:34.206
because when we got it, when we
screen-tested and we got it,

00:04:34.206 --> 00:04:36.075
I go, "Mom, I got it."
"You got what?"

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:38.110
"I'm on 'Sex Crimes.'"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:41.547
She's like,
"Can they change the name?"

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:44.150
-Did you have to say,
"Trying to catch them;

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.885
I play one of the guys
trying to catch them"?

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.287
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:48.654
-Exactly, yeah.
"I'm the good guy."

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.823
-And then she called Dick,
and he did change the name.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:51.690
-Exactly.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:52.925
-Did it ever air
as "Sex Crimes"?

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:55.127
-No, no, no.
-Never? Okay, gotcha.

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:58.197
-We were actually beginning to
do a little publicity for it,

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:00.066
and one of the publicists
ran up to us --

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:02.368
We're doing
whatever publicity line.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.902
-Yeah.
-And I said, you know,

00:05:03.902 --> 00:05:06.972
"It's great to be working on
the new show 'Sex Crimes.'"

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:09.541
And she came running up,

00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:11.744
"Hey, don't ever say
those words again!"

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.279
[ Laughter ]
"SVU."

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:15.314
-Nobody will watch a show called
"Sex Crimes."

00:05:15.314 --> 00:05:17.549
-So, "Law &amp; Order" is obviously
a franchise at this point,

00:05:17.549 --> 00:05:19.918
so you know that it has
a certain weight to be

00:05:19.918 --> 00:05:21.253
auditioning for
a Dick Wolf show.

00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:22.689
Do you remember being nervous
at the time like,

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:24.557
"Oh, this could be --" I mean,
no one thinks this could be

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.225
a show that is on
for 20-plus years.

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:27.827
But did you think,
"Oh, this might be actual --

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:29.828
you know, it's kind of
a normal job"?

00:05:29.828 --> 00:05:33.232
-Well, yeah, I thought --
You never think,

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:35.201
after being a struggling actor
for so long,

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:36.902
that any show is going to go.
-Right.

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:40.973
-But this was a unique audition
for us because when we met,

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:42.341
there was a certain chemistry,

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:45.311
so I actually wasn't nervous
at the audition.

00:05:46.278 --> 00:05:49.549
But you never think what
happened would happen.

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.584
You can't -- You can't dream it,
quite frankly.

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:53.385
-Do you want to re-enact
how that happened?

00:05:53.385 --> 00:05:54.787
-Yeah.
-If you do.

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:56.822
-Sure, go ahead.
What's the best camera?

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:59.391
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:59.391 --> 00:06:00.426
Is this good?
-This is real.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.960
This is what happened.
You ready?

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.429
Alright, ready?

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:07.699
-So, I open the door to the
audition, and I go like this.

00:06:07.699 --> 00:06:09.201
-Slattery!

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:10.403
-Meloni!

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:12.705
-And it was that.
[ Audience awws ]

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:14.440
-Wow.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:19.912
-I had heard that John Slattery
was testing for the part.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:23.149
-The guy who did "Mad Men."
-And I was so excited.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.483
Never met him.
-Yeah.

00:06:24.483 --> 00:06:26.953
-And he comes in, and so I knew
the other two guys,

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:28.488
so I knew that
they weren't Slattery.

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:30.223
And I see him and I go,
"Slattery,"

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:31.890
and he just goes, "Meloni!"

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:33.325
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.325 --> 00:06:36.595
I know Slattery,
and it's a big whiff to think --

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:38.898
-It's a different guy, right?
-Real different guy.

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.499
It's not like you're ever like,
"Those two,

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:43.236
you can't tell those two apart,"
because you definitely can.

00:06:43.236 --> 00:06:44.836
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.836 --> 00:06:47.106
-And yet Slattery and I would
have been great together.

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:49.708
Right?
-I hate to spend today making it

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:52.011
about that, but you guys would
have been great together.

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:53.345
-Whatever.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:55.414
-Noooo!
-No, no, no, no, no.

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:56.815
We're so happy it ended up
this way.

00:06:56.815 --> 00:06:58.885
I have so much more to ask.
-It was in the cards.

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:00.419
-We will be right back with more

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:02.522
from Mariska Hargitay
and Christopher Meloni.

